stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Initiated: Authority: GET /dataset/{gateId}/{platformId}/{datasetId}?subsetId=EU07

    Initiated --> LocalFetch: uil.gateId == this gate\n(eu-ee31 == eu-ee31)

    Initiated --> RemoteForward: uil.gateId != this gate\n(eu-ee31 != eu-fi01)

    LocalFetch --> PlatformRequest: Gate sends HTTP GET\nto local platform baseUrl

    RemoteForward --> GateForward: Gate sends UILQuery\nvia eDelivery AS4 or Fast HTTP\nto remote gate

    GateForward --> PlatformRequest: Remote gate fetches\nfrom its local platform

    PlatformRequest --> Approved: Platform returns 200 OK\nwith dataset XML

    PlatformRequest --> Denied: Platform returns 403 Forbidden\n(access denied for this subset)

    PlatformRequest --> NotFound: Platform returns 404 Not Found\n(dataset expired or deleted)

    PlatformRequest --> Error: Platform returns 5xx\nor connection timeout

    Approved --> Returned: Gate returns 200 OK\nwith dataset XML to authority

    Denied --> Returned: Gate returns 403 Forbidden\nto authority

    NotFound --> Returned: Gate returns 404 Not Found\nto authority

    Error --> Returned: Gate returns 502 Bad Gateway\nto authority

    Returned --> [*]

    RemoteForward --> GateUnavailable: checkGateAvailable() fails\n(gate.status != ONLINE)

    GateUnavailable --> Returned: 502 Bad Gateway\n"Cannot reach Gate eu-fi01: OFFLINE"

    note right of RemoteForward
        Routing decision based on UIL.gateId:
        - Same gate → direct platform call
        - Different gate → forward via eDelivery
        Gate status checked before forwarding.
    end note

    note right of Approved
        Authority receives full dataset XML
        filtered to requested subset (EU07, full, etc.)
        X-Request-ID header echoed in response.
    end note
